BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-178471@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260409T005935Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260410T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260410T183000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "The Best Dog in the World" with Alice Hoffman
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent U
 RL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/178471\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5
 :30PM Discussion\nFor anyone who has ever loved a dog\, the bond needs lit
 tle explanation. Join us for an intimate evening with bestselling author A
 lice Hoffman\, whose work so often explores the depths of love\, connectio
 n\, and what it means to care deeply—for one another and for the animals
  who share our lives.\n\nDrawing from her new essay collection\, The Best
  Dog in the World: Essays on Love\, Hoffman reflects on the joy\, loyalty\
 , and quiet wisdom our canine companions bring. Featuring contributions fr
 om an extraordinary group of writers\, the collection is a heartfelt tribu
 te to the dogs who leave lasting imprints on our lives.\n\nThe conversatio
 n will be moderated by Mike Travis\, Chief Development Officer of MSPCA-
 Angell\, one of the nation’s leading animal welfare and veterinary care 
 organizations. Founded in 1868\, MSPCA-Angell has long been at the forefro
 nt of animal protection and compassionate care—an institution with which
  Hoffman shares a personal connection\, having entrusted them with the car
 e of her own dogs over the years.\n\nWarm\, thoughtful\, and deeply resona
 nt\, this conversation offers a moving exploration of companionship\, empa
 thy\, and the enduring bond between people and their animals.\n\n*This eve
 nt is complimentary and reserved for members only. Light bites and refresh
 ments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/178471
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
