BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-179437@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260409T005935Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260412T164500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260412T193000
SUMMARY:Sunday Screening & Panel Discussion: FUEGO
LOCATION:The Living Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent U
 RL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/179437\n\n4:45PM Doors Open\, 
 5:00PM Screening\, 6:30PM Panel Discussion\nA gripping dramatic thriller a
 nd deeply human portrait\, join us for an intimate screening of FUEGO �
 � a film unveiled first at the United Nations General Assembly\, and now p
 rivately in the Living Room at The ‘Quin. The film sheds light on one of
  the most urgent yet overlooked humanitarian crises of our time tracing th
 e perilous journey faced by hundreds of thousands of Indigenous children f
 leeing the Northern Triangle of Central America\, revealing the harsh real
 ities that await many upon arrival in the United States.\n\nIn director Ar
 turo Muyshondt’s FUEGO\, a Mayan mother in the highlands of Guatemala f
 ights to protect her family as a devastating migration crisis upends her v
 illage. As instability spreads\, families are forced into impossible decis
 ions—risking everything for the chance at safety\, dignity\, and a futur
 e beyond survival.\n\nShaped by Muyshondt’s own experience growing up du
 ring the Salvadoran Civil War\, the film reflects a lifelong commitment to
  documenting the stories of migrant and war-affected children. Through FU
 EGO\, he positions cinema not only as storytelling\, but as a catalyst for
  awareness and change.\n\nFollowing the screening\, members are invited to
  remain for a thoughtful panel and audience Q&A featuring director and Co
 -Founder of the CARAS Foundation\, Arturo Muyshondt alongside Gabrielle Ol
 iveira\, Associate Professor of Education and of Brazil Studies at Harvard
  Graduate School of Education (HGSE)\, and Timothy Patrick McCarthy\, an a
 ward-winning scholar\, educator\, human rights activist and Lecturer on Ed
 ucation at HGSE. This special screening offers an opportunity to engage wi
 th a powerful work at the intersection of art and advocacy—one that seek
 s not only to illuminate\, but to inspire action.\n\n*This event is compli
 mentary and reserved for members only. Theatre fare and refreshments will 
 be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/179437
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
